<header><p class="st-kicker">princely state · Indian princely states</p><h1 class="st-title">Basoda State</h1><p class="st-meta">1753 CE – 1948 CE (approx.) · capital Basoda</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A small Pathan Nawabi state in Malwa, a branch of the family that ruled Kurwai.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Basoda was founded around 1753 by a member of the Afghan family of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kurwai-state">Kurwai</a>, one of several Pathan chiefships established in the area during the decline of Mughal power.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The Nawab ruled a small farming territory around the town of Basoda in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bhopal-agency">Bhopal Agency</a>. Few details of its internal history are recorded.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>After accession to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a> Basoda was merged into <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/madhya-bharat">Madhya Bharat</a> in 1948 and joined <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/madhya-pradesh">Madhya Pradesh</a> in 1956; its lands are in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vidisha">Vidisha</a> district.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/basoda-state.jpg" alt="Basoda State" width="320" height="197"><figcaption>Image: Great Britain India Office · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Basoda-Muhammadgarh_map.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1753 CE – 1948 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>princely state</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Basoda</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Hinduism; Sunni Islam (ruling house)</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Malvi, Hindi</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/india">India</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Basoda</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1850&amp;focus=basoda-state" aria-label="Basoda State on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="6756 1299 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Basoda State lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M7076 1555L7364 1601M7076 1555L7364 1602M7076 1555L7018 1386"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M7364 1601h0M7364 1602h0M7018 1386h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M7076 1555h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M7076 1555h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks its recorded location. <a href="/atlas?year=1850&amp;focus=basoda-state">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
